window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>The plan is finally set: a divine, multi-pronged ambush targeting Providence where it's weakest.</b></p> <p>Five gods. Five demons. Five simultaneous strategic executions. Against a brutal corporate autocracy, the odds are worth the risk.</p> <p>But even as deities start falling, it becomes clear the company hasn't given up all its secrets. In the opening left behind, background forces converge, exposing other plans than Loki's. With the balance of power crashing, creation steers with it.</p> <p>Now, Loki must defeat his target, grapple with multiple shifting fronts, and outwit prophecy yet again. All the threads are finally coming back together. Unfortunately, so is his reputation.</p> <p>And that's when things start getting complicated.</p> <p>Deicide <i>forms the epic conclusion of Doing God's Work, combining mythology, blasphemy, and rebellion in this sacrilegious corporate fantasy.</i></p>"; 
